  "id": "Compound::DB00748 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Carbinoxamine, through its inclusion in the Histamine H1 Receptor Antagonists class, binds to Cyp3a4. This is supported by multiple pathways where Carbinoxamine is linked to different members of the Histamine H1 Receptor Antagonists group, all of which ultimately bind to Cyp3a4. The lowest common ancestors of these pathways—Carbinoxamine and the respective antagonists—point to shared molecular characteristics, such as being tertiary amino compounds or organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds, which may facilitate binding to Cyp3a4. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support across different antagonists. The integration of these pathways suggests that Carbinoxamine may influence Cyp3a4 through a common mechanism involving histamine receptor antagonism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains partially uncertain.",
